"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, the_escapists_2.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. BepInEx will then be downloaded into the game's core files, along with the AP Mod folder, which will be placed in BepInEx\\plugins.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"TE2 is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'the_escapists_2.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, a new AP Connection bridge window will open separately at the same time as the game. Once inside the game's main menu, click 'Play Game' and then go to the window called 'The EscAPists 2 Bridge' that opened with the game.\n\nIt will ask you to enter your 'Slot Name', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThen, it will ask you to type the 'Server Address'. You'll have to type archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nLast thing should be the 'Password' it is optional, just press ENTER if the host didn't set one.\n\nFinally, go back to the game and you should be able to start playing!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for The Escapists 2 Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear BepInEx' option it will delete everything related to BepInEx and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
